  "details": "If I put the viewpoint for the eye position between the eyes on the nose on the avi in Unity. Ill load the avi in VRChat and calibrate my FBT if I stand up the viewpoint is the correct height but a bit to far to the front (I'm using a Quest 2 with vive FBT). If I am gonna sit down on my chair or ground and check my viewpoint again I noticed the camera for the viewpoint is lower that it should be like from eye height (what is good) to mouth or even chin height (what is bad) on the avi. So the calculation for the position is not right in the SDK for the eye viewpoint. I noticed this bug for a few month now but nobody reported it. Please investigate this. Me as a dancer is relying a lot on my viewpoint position. It started braking when the avi height adjustment was implemented in VRChat.",
